Package: SplitAlignerR
Title: Split-Based Branch Mapping and Coordinate Auditing for Phylogenomics
Version: 0.0.1
Authors@R:
    person("Jiaqi", "Wu", email = "wujiaqi@hiroshima-u.ac.jp", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: An R implementation, currently a scaffold, of the SplitAligner
    branch-identity coordinate system for phylogenomics under missing taxa and
    gene-tree discordance. This release ships the deterministic Catnip10 10-tip
    coordinate-audit benchmark expected oracle outputs as bundled data and a
    placeholder function so the package installs and checks cleanly. The
    split-based branch-mapping engine will be added in later versions. See the
    SplitAligner preprint (Wu 2026, <doi:10.64898/2026.02.24.707838>).
License: GPL-3
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends:
    R (>= 3.5.0)
Imports:
    utils
Suggests:
    testthat (>= 3.0.0)
Config/testthat/edition: 3
